WEBVTT

00:00:04.350 --> 00:00:06.360
<i>I want ramen.</i>

00:00:08.310 --> 00:00:09.700
<i>Ramen...</i>

00:00:11.080 --> 00:00:12.590
<i>Ramen...</i>

00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:16.990
<i>I want ramen.</i>

00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:21.410
Here you go.

00:00:23.790 --> 00:00:24.960
<i>She...</i>

00:00:25.630 --> 00:00:26.920
Time to eat.

00:00:27.180 --> 00:00:31.440
<i>...will surely be eating
ramen once again today.</i>

00:00:37.010 --> 00:00:42.020
<b>Ms. Koizumi
Loves Ramen
Noodles</b>

00:00:59.780 --> 00:01:00.490
<b>Loves Ramen
Noodles</b>

00:01:00.490 --> 00:01:01.040
<b>Ms. Koizumi</b>

00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:01.950
<b>Ms. Koizumi
Loves Ramen
Noodles</b>

00:02:13.070 --> 00:02:16.990
<b>Garlic With Extra Vegetables</b>

00:02:13.350 --> 00:02:17.770
In literary history terms, we would
classify this work in the "zuihitsu" genre.

00:02:17.770 --> 00:02:20.730
But at the time, there was no such concept.

00:02:20.730 --> 00:02:24.740
She could be called the 
first to write in that style.

00:02:41.370 --> 00:02:43.630
<i>She's so cute.</i>

00:02:43.630 --> 00:02:44.790
Ohsawa-san?

00:02:44.790 --> 00:02:45.780
Y-Yes?!

00:02:45.780 --> 00:02:48.000
Read the next part, please.

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:49.970
Um...

00:02:51.520 --> 00:02:53.360
Sorry.

00:02:53.360 --> 00:02:56.760
By the way, that's your math textbook.

00:02:57.480 --> 00:02:59.560
Settle down, everyone.

00:02:59.560 --> 00:03:01.190
Okay, then, can I get...

00:03:01.190 --> 00:03:02.490
Actually, Ohsawa-san...

00:03:05.880 --> 00:03:07.200
Yuu!

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:08.700
Jeez, Misa.

00:03:08.700 --> 00:03:10.920
Hee-hee. You got in trouble.

00:03:10.920 --> 00:03:12.090
What were you looking at?

00:03:12.090 --> 00:03:13.180
Well...

00:03:13.180 --> 00:03:14.920
That new transfer student?

00:03:14.920 --> 00:03:17.270
Koizumi-san, was it?

00:03:17.270 --> 00:03:18.860
Jeez, Jun!

00:03:18.860 --> 00:03:21.900
I don't really like her.

00:03:21.900 --> 00:03:23.140
Why not?

00:03:23.140 --> 00:03:28.010
She hasn't tried to talk to anyone 
since she moved here.

00:03:28.010 --> 00:03:30.880
She's just, like, kind of cold.

00:03:30.880 --> 00:03:32.850
I haven't talked to her yet, either.

00:03:33.980 --> 00:03:36.160
I haven't either, actually.

00:03:36.160 --> 00:03:38.320
But I'm kind of curious about her.

00:03:39.390 --> 00:03:42.690
You've always loved cute girls, Yuu.

00:03:42.690 --> 00:03:44.970
You have a cute girl right here.

00:03:44.970 --> 00:03:47.140
No one could be cuter than me!

00:03:47.140 --> 00:03:48.650
Sure, sure...

00:03:48.650 --> 00:03:50.120
You're cute, too, Misa.

00:03:50.120 --> 00:03:50.960
"Too"?!

00:03:53.070 --> 00:03:55.320
Hey, let's go clothes shopping.

00:03:55.320 --> 00:03:56.380
I have cram school.

00:03:56.380 --> 00:03:57.960
Sorry, I'm going home, too.

00:03:57.960 --> 00:03:59.700
I'm supposed to make dinner tonight.

00:04:00.970 --> 00:04:02.590
<b>Pedestrians and
bicycles only</b>

00:04:03.180 --> 00:04:03.980
See you.

00:04:03.980 --> 00:04:04.400
See you.

00:04:04.400 --> 00:04:05.100
Bye.

00:04:09.180 --> 00:04:11.320
<i>Sorry, I have overtime today.</i>

00:04:11.320 --> 00:04:13.170
<i>Can you all make dinner for yourselves?</i>

00:04:13.170 --> 00:04:14.220
<i>Heart!</i>

00:04:14.220 --> 00:04:16.080
<i>I don't need dinner tonight, either.</i>

00:04:16.080 --> 00:04:17.020
Uh-oh...

00:04:17.380 --> 00:04:19.820
What do I do for dinner now?

00:04:20.300 --> 00:04:22.090
Convenience store, I guess?

00:04:23.300 --> 00:04:26.120
<i>That shop's got a huge line again.</i>

00:04:27.070 --> 00:04:30.530
<i>And it doesn't even look like 
it's open yet. It's so popular.</i>

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:34.250
<b>Ramen</b>

00:04:31.920 --> 00:04:34.250
<i>Ramen, huh?</i>

00:04:34.490 --> 00:04:38.300
<i>I'd like some, but I don't know about 
a girl going out for ramen by herself.</i>

00:04:48.640 --> 00:04:51.180
<i>Koizumi-san?!</i>

00:04:52.830 --> 00:04:55.160
<i>Why is she here by herself?</i>

00:04:55.160 --> 00:04:56.960
Um, are you in line here?

00:04:57.780 --> 00:05:01.800
Oh, um...

00:05:04.830 --> 00:05:05.710
Yes.

00:05:07.850 --> 00:05:10.600
<i>What is even going on here?</i>

00:05:11.580 --> 00:05:14.780
<i>Oh, well. I do like ramen.</i>

00:05:14.780 --> 00:05:15.960
<i>That aside...</i>

00:05:16.570 --> 00:05:18.460
<i>Her hair's so pretty.</i>

00:05:18.960 --> 00:05:20.960
<i>And her skin's so pale.</i>

00:05:21.590 --> 00:05:23.590
<i>And her lashes are so long!</i>

00:05:24.500 --> 00:05:28.720
<i>Koizumi-san is so pretty up close.</i>

00:05:29.270 --> 00:05:32.420
<i>I never got to talk to her until now,
 but this is my chance.</i>

00:05:32.420 --> 00:05:34.880
Hey, Koizumi-san, do you remember me?

00:05:34.880 --> 00:05:37.220
I'm Ohsawa Yuu, from your class.

00:05:37.220 --> 00:05:38.560
I'm a Leo, blood type O.

00:05:38.560 --> 00:05:39.310
Nice to meet you.

00:05:39.750 --> 00:05:43.190
I never knew you ate ramen by yourself.

00:05:43.190 --> 00:05:45.440
It's not something one does with a group.

00:05:49.200 --> 00:05:50.400
Wow!

00:05:50.400 --> 00:05:53.190
I can't help but worry about 
what other people think.

00:05:53.190 --> 00:05:55.160
Do you come to this restaurant often?

00:05:53.330 --> 00:05:55.160
<b>Never lose heart
Never back down
Never give up
—Yuu</b>

00:05:55.160 --> 00:05:58.790
<b>Silence</b>

00:05:57.540 --> 00:05:58.790
<i>She's not even listening.</i>

00:06:00.300 --> 00:06:01.620
Thanks for waiting.

00:06:01.620 --> 00:06:03.210
Looks like they're opening.

00:06:14.220 --> 00:06:16.680
Food tickets? It's like the school cafeteria.

00:06:16.680 --> 00:06:18.190
Okay, I'll have the same one.

00:06:18.190 --> 00:06:20.310
<b>Pork Double
Ramen</b>

00:06:18.190 --> 00:06:21.020
<b>Yen</b>

00:06:21.020 --> 00:06:23.400
<b>Pork Double
Ramen</b>

00:06:27.960 --> 00:06:31.030
<i>I've never been to a ramen 
shop after school before.</i>

00:06:31.450 --> 00:06:33.640
Would you like garlic in yours?

00:06:34.190 --> 00:06:36.790
Extra vegetables,
with garlic oil, medium-hot.

00:06:37.140 --> 00:06:38.320
<i>Say what?!</i>

00:06:38.320 --> 00:06:39.100
Okay.

00:06:39.100 --> 00:06:41.240
And for you? Would you like garlic?

00:06:41.880 --> 00:06:42.790
Yes!

00:06:43.040 --> 00:06:45.150
Give me, like, the same thing.

00:06:45.150 --> 00:06:46.540
Understood.

00:06:49.840 --> 00:06:52.960
Here's your medium-hot pork double 
with extra vegetables and garlic oil.

00:06:52.960 --> 00:06:55.810
<i>It's a mountain of meat and sprouts!</i>

00:06:56.480 --> 00:06:58.810
<i>I can't see the noodles!</i>

00:06:59.970 --> 00:07:02.140
Hey, is this...

00:07:05.900 --> 00:07:09.340
Here's your medium-hot pork double 
with extra vegetables and garlic oil.

00:07:11.970 --> 00:07:13.400
Time to eat.

00:07:58.070 --> 00:07:58.900
<i>Wh—</i>

00:08:00.020 --> 00:08:00.980
<i>Wha—</i>

00:08:02.060 --> 00:08:03.750
<i>What the hell was that?!</i>

00:08:04.130 --> 00:08:08.130
<i>And she looks so blissful!</i>

00:08:11.070 --> 00:08:13.130
<i>Oh, she's back to normal.</i>

00:08:13.970 --> 00:08:15.270
Yours will get soggy.

00:08:29.570 --> 00:08:30.530
<b>Urp</b>

00:08:29.570 --> 00:08:30.530
<b>Done.</b>

00:08:30.920 --> 00:08:32.540
That was so much...

00:08:32.540 --> 00:08:36.740
I'm going to have ramen coming 
out of every orifice in my body.

00:08:37.160 --> 00:08:39.400
I thought you were a regular.

00:08:39.400 --> 00:08:41.370
That was my first time.

00:08:42.450 --> 00:08:44.700
Okay, I'm going now.

00:08:46.010 --> 00:08:48.210
Hey, Koizumi-san...

00:08:48.930 --> 00:08:51.090
You really like ramen, huh?

00:08:57.990 --> 00:08:59.310
I do.

00:09:04.230 --> 00:09:08.590
<i>She's very composed, but she might actually 
be a normal, down-to-earth girl.</i>

00:09:08.590 --> 00:09:12.080
Well, if you know any good places, 
tell me about them sometime.

00:09:12.080 --> 00:09:13.760
No, thank you.

00:09:13.760 --> 00:09:18.200
Is it, like, you want to keep the 
best places a secret for yourself?

00:09:19.260 --> 00:09:23.250
Come on, we're classmates now.

00:09:23.250 --> 00:09:25.560
We should talk more.

00:09:25.560 --> 00:09:27.670
About ramen or anything else.

00:09:32.450 --> 00:09:34.210
No, thank you.

00:09:40.630 --> 00:09:44.400
<i>This is the story of a 
ramen lover, Koizumi-san.</i>

00:09:49.970 --> 00:09:52.650
Koizumi-san, walking through 
a flurry of cherry blossoms...

00:09:52.650 --> 00:09:54.500
So picturesque!

00:09:54.500 --> 00:09:57.560
All right, I'll try talking 
to her again tomorrow.

00:09:58.160 --> 00:09:59.870
<b>One Week Later</b>

00:10:02.560 --> 00:10:03.870
<i>Why?</i>

00:10:04.670 --> 00:10:08.000
<i>I want that ramen again.</i>

00:10:11.500 --> 00:10:14.000
<b>Ms. Koizumi
Loves Ramen
Noodles</b>

00:10:15.090 --> 00:10:19.010
<b>Maayu</b>

00:10:25.410 --> 00:10:27.130
I'm so hungry.

00:10:27.130 --> 00:10:28.540
What do you want for lunch?

00:10:28.540 --> 00:10:31.480
Something light, maybe?

00:10:32.770 --> 00:10:34.780
<b>Yummy!</b>

00:10:33.010 --> 00:10:34.780
Koizumi-san!

00:10:34.780 --> 00:10:39.400
<b>New Menu</b>

00:10:35.400 --> 00:10:36.870
What are you looking at?

00:10:37.600 --> 00:10:39.870
Wait, don't run from me!

00:10:40.920 --> 00:10:42.900
Was that Koizumi?

00:10:44.080 --> 00:10:45.010
Jeez.

00:10:45.010 --> 00:10:47.910
We ate ramen together,
but she's still so cold to me.

00:10:47.910 --> 00:10:49.520
What was she looking at?

00:10:48.410 --> 00:10:50.870
<b>New Menu</b>

00:10:48.410 --> 00:10:56.050
<b>Original
Maayu</b>

00:10:49.950 --> 00:10:51.780
Horse oil?

00:10:52.220 --> 00:10:56.050
Koizumi-san sure does love ramen.

00:10:56.490 --> 00:10:59.320
Hey, want to have lunch in the 
school cafeteria for once?

00:10:59.320 --> 00:11:00.560
I want ramen.

00:11:00.560 --> 00:11:02.470
That's not light at all.

00:11:02.470 --> 00:11:04.160
No way. It's too crowded.

00:11:04.160 --> 00:11:05.640
I'm just going to buy some bread.

00:11:05.640 --> 00:11:07.600
I don't like ramen, anyway.

00:11:07.600 --> 00:11:09.040
Why?!

00:11:09.040 --> 00:11:13.170
You have to help me with "Operation: 
Make Friends With Koizumi-san"!

00:11:13.060 --> 00:11:14.900
<b>Never even heard of it</b>

00:11:13.170 --> 00:11:14.900
I don't care about that.

00:11:16.740 --> 00:11:18.030
What about you, Misa?

00:11:18.030 --> 00:11:21.450
What do you like about that antisocial girl?

00:11:21.450 --> 00:11:24.160
That's what's awesome about her.

00:11:24.400 --> 00:11:27.370
I hate everyone who's more popular than me.

00:11:27.370 --> 00:11:28.300
That's all.

00:11:28.300 --> 00:11:30.540
There, there, don't be jealous.

00:11:30.540 --> 00:11:33.000
You're cute enough, Misa.

00:11:33.000 --> 00:11:34.290
Who's cuter, me or Koizumi?

00:11:34.290 --> 00:11:35.130
Koizumi-san.

00:11:35.130 --> 00:11:36.090
Hey!

00:11:36.610 --> 00:11:38.750
<i>Another peaceful day.</i>

00:11:39.760 --> 00:11:42.130
Traitor!

00:11:42.130 --> 00:11:44.920
Okay, okay, let's go buy some bread.

00:11:44.920 --> 00:11:45.920
What kind do you want?

00:11:45.920 --> 00:11:47.180
A cream bun.

00:11:50.460 --> 00:11:51.850
Can I sit next to you?

00:11:52.620 --> 00:11:54.230
You again?

00:11:54.700 --> 00:11:56.920
You can do as you please.

00:11:56.920 --> 00:11:59.300
This isn't my house.

00:11:59.300 --> 00:12:01.360
Then I shall do so!

00:12:01.360 --> 00:12:03.640
You got the same thing I did.

00:12:03.640 --> 00:12:06.620
This is my first time having Kumamoto ramen.

00:12:15.230 --> 00:12:16.590
Thank you for the food.

00:12:16.850 --> 00:12:20.170
You didn't eat in a hurry 
like you did last time.

00:12:20.170 --> 00:12:26.510
I eat faster at that restaurant to avoid 
dragging down the customer turnover.

00:12:27.100 --> 00:12:28.310
<b>Turnover?</b>

00:12:27.100 --> 00:12:28.610
Huh...

00:12:28.610 --> 00:12:32.140
Oh, hey, is this ramen made with tonkotsu?

00:12:32.140 --> 00:12:34.440
It has a unique scent, though.

00:12:34.780 --> 00:12:38.190
I wonder if it's this black stuff 
that's floating in the soup.

00:12:38.190 --> 00:12:40.360
Oh, I know!

00:12:40.360 --> 00:12:42.240
<b>Original
Maayu</b>

00:12:40.360 --> 00:12:43.490
It's the "horse oil" that 
was written on the board.

00:12:44.360 --> 00:12:45.340
That must be it!

00:12:45.340 --> 00:12:47.570
It's the horse oil giving it that flavor!

00:12:47.960 --> 00:12:51.750
I never knew horse oil worked 
so well in tonkotsu soup.

00:12:51.750 --> 00:12:54.900
It's a miraculous collaboration 
between horse and pig!

00:12:54.900 --> 00:12:57.200
Man, horse oil is great!

00:12:57.200 --> 00:12:58.130
"Maayu."

00:12:59.180 --> 00:13:02.800
It's not "horse oil." It's read "maayu."

00:13:03.910 --> 00:13:08.010
Unlike the horse oil that's 
used in cosmetics and such,

00:13:08.500 --> 00:13:11.170
"maayu" in ramen refers to a 
seasoning that's made by

00:13:11.170 --> 00:13:13.680
burning garlic and 
transferring its fragrance.

00:13:13.680 --> 00:13:15.600
It has nothing to do with horses?

00:13:15.910 --> 00:13:17.900
If anything, it would be chicken.

00:13:17.900 --> 00:13:22.210
<b>Kumamoto Style
Uses maayu in broth,
topped with jelly ear</b>

00:13:18.380 --> 00:13:22.170
Kumamoto-style ramen uses a mix 
of tonkotsu and chicken broth.

00:13:22.170 --> 00:13:24.920
By adding maayu, they give it 
a richness that sets it apart

00:13:24.280 --> 00:13:27.530
<b>Kumamoto Style
Uses maayu in broth,
topped with jelly ear</b>

00:13:24.280 --> 00:13:27.530
<b>Kurume Style
The root of almost
all Kyushu ramen</b>

00:13:24.280 --> 00:13:27.530
<b>Tamana Style
Origin of Kumamoto ramen,
topped with garlic chips</b>

00:13:24.920 --> 00:13:27.530
from the Kurume and Tamana
styles that it's based on.

00:13:27.530 --> 00:13:32.290
But perhaps because it's a school cafeteria, 
they've gone easy on the garlic.

00:13:32.600 --> 00:13:36.880
Authentic maayu has a much 
stronger garlic smell.

00:13:36.880 --> 00:13:40.040
It's also customary to 
include fried garlic chips.

00:13:40.340 --> 00:13:44.130
<i>She'll actually talk to me when 
it's about something she likes.</i>

00:13:40.340 --> 00:13:44.920
Hakata and Nagahama ramen are the most 
mainstream Kyushu tonkotsu styles,

00:13:44.920 --> 00:13:48.260
but Kumamoto style is known 
for its thicker noodles.

00:13:48.260 --> 00:13:49.430
Huh...

00:13:48.260 --> 00:13:50.990
They're most commonly prepared to be firmer.

00:13:50.990 --> 00:13:53.910
When I eat there, I ask for it firm.

00:13:53.910 --> 00:13:57.010
<i>She has such a cute, feminine voice.</i>

00:13:58.860 --> 00:14:03.840
<i>Koizumi-san went to Kumamoto 
to have ramen, huh?</i>

00:14:06.070 --> 00:14:09.460
There's a new shop near the school.

00:14:09.460 --> 00:14:11.230
Yeah? And?

00:14:12.430 --> 00:14:13.750
Hey!

00:14:13.750 --> 00:14:16.240
I want to try the ramen there!

00:14:16.240 --> 00:14:18.020
Want to go there sometime?

00:14:22.200 --> 00:14:23.370
I do not.

00:14:32.160 --> 00:14:33.440
<i>Score!</i>

00:14:33.440 --> 00:14:36.020
<i>I got to talk to her a lot today!</i>

00:14:36.520 --> 00:14:40.480
<b>New Menu!!
With Chiiyu
Solid Iekei</b>

00:14:37.970 --> 00:14:40.480
Now it's chicken oil, huh?

00:14:40.850 --> 00:14:43.480
<i>Wait, it's gonna turn out that 
there's no chicken in it, isn't it?!</i>

00:14:43.750 --> 00:14:45.280
Close call.

00:14:44.900 --> 00:14:46.940
<b>Chiiyu
Seasoning made from chicken skin</b>

00:14:45.280 --> 00:14:46.940
It's "chiiyu."

00:14:49.450 --> 00:14:51.950
<b>Ms. Koizumi
Loves Ramen
Noodles</b>

00:14:55.660 --> 00:14:59.580
<b>Rich</b>

00:15:02.820 --> 00:15:07.170
<i>Koizumi-san is at a ramen shop again.</i>

00:15:09.260 --> 00:15:12.370
<i>Koizumi-san takes a seat,
and immediately makes an order.</i>

00:15:12.370 --> 00:15:13.510
Karaage combo, please.

00:15:13.800 --> 00:15:17.930
We have three soup flavors: 
rich, light, and stall-style.

00:15:18.440 --> 00:15:22.960
<i>Without hesitation, Koizumi-san chooses rich,
with a karaage meal on the side.</i>

00:15:22.960 --> 00:15:25.820
<i>She eats more than she looks like she would.</i>

00:15:25.820 --> 00:15:29.570
<i>She ties her beautiful hair back, 
perfectly prepared for battle.</i>

00:15:31.000 --> 00:15:32.140
Time to eat.

00:15:32.140 --> 00:15:33.900
<i>Yup, time to eat.</i>

00:15:34.930 --> 00:15:38.080
<i>This is even richer than expected.</i>

00:15:38.080 --> 00:15:40.900
<i>The noodles are covered in the muddy soup.</i>

00:15:41.540 --> 00:15:42.960
<i>So muddy...</i>

00:15:59.130 --> 00:16:04.520
<i>Koizumi-san looks incredibly 
happy when she's eating ramen.</i>

00:16:05.260 --> 00:16:07.530
Excuse me. Would you 
please stop watching me?

00:16:07.530 --> 00:16:08.760
Oh, shoot!

00:16:08.760 --> 00:16:11.610
I was so mesmerized, my inner 
play-by-play shut off for a moment.

00:16:12.040 --> 00:16:13.990
Why are you here?

00:16:14.780 --> 00:16:17.120
I don't remember coming here with you.

00:16:18.670 --> 00:16:20.250
You just noticed?

00:16:20.820 --> 00:16:24.490
Remember when I saw you at the school 
gate and approached you?

00:16:22.890 --> 00:16:26.710
Koizumi-san, let's walk home together!

00:16:25.420 --> 00:16:26.710
And you ignored me.

00:16:27.240 --> 00:16:29.090
I had no choice,

00:16:29.090 --> 00:16:34.780
so I kind of casually followed you,
and came to this restaurant.

00:16:36.260 --> 00:16:40.390
I totally didn't think you'd 
switch trains just to get ramen.

00:16:40.390 --> 00:16:42.670
Please stop stalking me.

00:16:48.400 --> 00:16:50.200
The ramen's so good.

00:16:51.190 --> 00:16:55.380
This soup is really thick, though, isn't it?

00:16:55.380 --> 00:16:57.030
I can't place this texture.

00:16:57.030 --> 00:16:58.830
It's a bit like white stew...

00:16:59.460 --> 00:17:02.240
Oh! It's like spaghetti carbonara!

00:17:02.240 --> 00:17:03.710
I had some at Saize last week.

00:17:04.050 --> 00:17:06.080
I've never had ramen like this.

00:17:06.080 --> 00:17:08.710
It's white soup, so I guess 
it must be tonkotsu ramen?

00:17:09.080 --> 00:17:13.460
It doesn't taste anything like that 
Kumamoto tonkotsu from before, though.

00:17:13.460 --> 00:17:14.360
Of course not.

00:17:14.880 --> 00:17:17.150
This soup uses chicken broth.

00:17:17.150 --> 00:17:21.850
You think all milky white soup
uses tonkotsu, don't you?

00:17:22.480 --> 00:17:23.850
It doesn't?

00:17:23.850 --> 00:17:27.080
To be honest, as someone 
who doesn't know too much,

00:17:27.080 --> 00:17:29.460
all I knew was that murky
white soup is tonkotsu,

00:17:29.460 --> 00:17:33.200
clear white soup is salt,
murky brown soup is miso,

00:17:33.200 --> 00:17:36.860
and clear brown is soy sauce.

00:17:37.290 --> 00:17:40.520
I can't believe you survived all this 
time with such little awareness.

00:17:40.520 --> 00:17:41.480
I'm impressed.

00:17:41.480 --> 00:17:43.460
But that's about normal!

00:17:43.460 --> 00:17:45.330
It's never caused any problems for me!

00:17:45.330 --> 00:17:54.340
<b>Broth

00:17:45.860 --> 00:17:50.080
Tonkotsu is classified as a broth.
Those others are classified as sauces.

00:17:46.710 --> 00:17:54.340
<b>Sauce

00:17:50.080 --> 00:17:52.050
Broth? Sauce?

00:17:51.250 --> 00:17:54.340
<b>Mix</b>

00:17:51.250 --> 00:17:54.340
<b>Complete soup</b>

00:17:52.050 --> 00:17:54.340
They're the basic elements of ramen soup.

00:17:54.340 --> 00:17:59.040
<b>Tsubame-Sanjou Style Ramen</b>

00:17:54.340 --> 00:17:59.040
<b>Hakata Tonkotsu Ramen, etc.</b>

00:17:54.340 --> 00:18:09.600
<b>Tonkotsu x Chicken Broth
+
Maayu</b>

00:17:54.340 --> 00:18:09.600
<b>Kumamoto Ramen, etc.</b>

00:17:54.340 --> 00:18:09.600
<b>Tonkotsu x Soy Sauce x Chicken Broth</b>

00:17:54.340 --> 00:18:09.600
<b>Iekei Tonkotsu Soy Sauce Ramen, etc.</b>

00:17:54.340 --> 00:18:09.600
<b>Seafood x Soy Sauce + Lard</b>

00:17:54.340 --> 00:18:09.600
<b>100% Tonkotsu Broth</b>

00:17:54.720 --> 00:17:56.890
The different broth and sauce combinations,

00:17:56.890 --> 00:17:59.040
as well as different seasonings,

00:17:59.040 --> 00:18:02.720
can create countless flavors, 
even for the same soup,

00:18:02.720 --> 00:18:05.610
that are difficult to name
using their bases alone.

00:18:05.610 --> 00:18:08.030
This is suddenly getting complicated.

00:18:08.030 --> 00:18:09.600
It's like a science experiment.

00:18:10.140 --> 00:18:13.480
This creamy soup uses 
chicken and vegetable broth.

00:18:13.480 --> 00:18:17.610
The texture comes from boiling 
that down until it becomes thick.

00:18:17.980 --> 00:18:20.900
That apparently makes it rich in collagen.

00:18:20.900 --> 00:18:21.990
Collagen?!

00:18:21.990 --> 00:18:26.080
<i>That</i> collagen, the one that
makes your skin all smooth?!

00:18:21.990 --> 00:18:26.750
<b>Smooth</b>

00:18:24.660 --> 00:18:26.750
<b>Beautiful!</b>

00:18:27.290 --> 00:18:29.460
I must drink all of this.

00:18:30.640 --> 00:18:32.230
But there's no soup!

00:18:32.230 --> 00:18:35.090
The noodles absorbed it all. 
There's no soup left!

00:18:35.410 --> 00:18:38.840
The noodles were soft to begin with,
and now they're just soggy.

00:18:39.140 --> 00:18:42.350
It's completely turned into carbonara!

00:18:43.400 --> 00:18:44.510
Yours too, Koizumi-san!

00:18:44.510 --> 00:18:48.530
Sorry! I ruined your ramen by pestering you!

00:18:48.530 --> 00:18:49.560
It's fine.

00:18:50.080 --> 00:18:51.940
I was waiting for this.

00:18:53.240 --> 00:18:56.030
As soon as it arrives,
I consume half of the noodles.

00:18:56.360 --> 00:19:00.160
I then leave the bowl for a while,
picking at the rice and side in the meantime.

00:19:00.530 --> 00:19:02.990
Once the noodles have completely 
soaked up the soup,

00:19:03.700 --> 00:19:05.350
I scarf it all down.

00:19:17.140 --> 00:19:20.260
This is my personal favorite way to enjoy it.

00:19:20.740 --> 00:19:25.910
Further, at shops that serve free boiled eggs,
I break them into the soup.

00:19:25.910 --> 00:19:28.670
The resulting flavor is 
indeed carbonara ramen.

00:19:28.670 --> 00:19:30.840
It's addictive enough that
I crave it once a week.

00:19:30.810 --> 00:19:32.270
<b>For real?!</b>

00:19:30.840 --> 00:19:32.270
That often?!

00:19:32.270 --> 00:19:34.400
<b>Please come back tomorrow.</b>

00:19:33.440 --> 00:19:37.500
<i>This is the story of a 
ramen lover, Koizumi-san.</i>

00:19:37.990 --> 00:19:40.280
Thanks for the meal.

00:19:44.360 --> 00:19:45.590
Morning.

00:19:45.590 --> 00:19:46.220
Morning.

00:19:46.220 --> 00:19:47.040
Morning.

00:19:47.710 --> 00:19:49.750
Koizumi-san!

00:19:50.360 --> 00:19:52.110
Morning!

00:19:52.910 --> 00:19:54.380
Hey, look.

00:19:54.380 --> 00:19:58.600
Don't you think my skin's gotten 
smoother from that collagen yesterday?

00:19:58.600 --> 00:19:59.440
Yesterday?

00:19:59.440 --> 00:20:01.630
You were with Koizumi-san, Yuu?

00:20:01.630 --> 00:20:04.640
Yeah, we had ramen together.

00:20:04.640 --> 00:20:07.600
It's not going to work overnight.

00:20:08.630 --> 00:20:11.260
It'll work if I eat it a few times, right?

00:20:11.260 --> 00:20:13.850
Let's go back today, Koizumi-san.

00:20:14.380 --> 00:20:16.040
No, thank you.

00:20:22.590 --> 00:20:24.060
What a jerk.

00:20:24.060 --> 00:20:26.840
I still don't like that girl.

00:20:26.840 --> 00:20:27.830
Yuu...

00:20:31.100 --> 00:20:32.280
Yay!

00:20:32.280 --> 00:20:35.020
I got to talk to Koizumi-san 
first thing in the morning!

00:20:35.020 --> 00:20:37.540
Today's going to be a good day!

00:20:37.540 --> 00:20:40.050
<i>There's no getting her down...</i>

00:22:10.010 --> 00:22:30.030
<b>Hokkyoku</b>

00:22:10.010 --> 00:22:30.030
<b>K-K-K-K-Koizumi-san</b>

00:22:12.840 --> 00:22:18.920
Hey, hey, Koizumi-san, it takes a lot of courage 
to walk into a ramen shop alone, doesn't it?

00:22:18.920 --> 00:22:22.360
You seem totally cool with doing that, though.

00:22:22.360 --> 00:22:24.090
You're so awesome!

00:22:24.090 --> 00:22:25.500
I admire you so much!

00:22:26.130 --> 00:22:27.780
Who were you, again?

00:22:27.780 --> 00:22:29.050
So cool!

00:22:30.030 --> 00:22:36.040
<b>Thank you for the meal...</b>
